CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ copy constructor ran once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ handler binds to the copy: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fixed: the THROW was lowered to a bitwise copy of the operand, so the
copy constructor never ran.  The front end now initializes a temporary
of the exception type from the operand through the selected constructor
(typecheck_expr_throw).
